#! ia 1.0

@playbook catalogue-author
  meaning
    says "How a plugin is authored for a catalogue: read the catalogue's house rules and its validator, plan the change within every rule, make it, run the validator through the catalogue-validate check, and have it reviewed by someone who did not write it. The rules are the catalogue-* conventions, each citing the symbol or message tools/validate.py or the manifest schema carries."
    answers "What does an agent do to add or change a plugin in a catalogue?"
  subject
    subject-word capability
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Read the plugin and the catalogue: the plugin's manifests, skills, agents and any hooks, and the catalogue's tools/validate.py and schemas/plugin-manifest.schema.json."
      Inference means "Read the nine catalogue conventions and check each against the validator's current text: a rule is cited by its symbol or message, never by a line number, and the validator is the truth when the two differ."
      Decision means "Decide whether the change is in scope: a plugin built from IA records goes through host-lower and host-project first; a new word, system, workspace or kit is out of this kit's scope (authoring-scope)."
      Learning means "Read the catalogue's earlier validator runs and review findings for this plugin."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate the budgets the change must fit: every skill description at most 400 characters with a use-when phrase, at most four model-invocable skills per plugin, hidden skill descriptions at most 160 characters, the whole catalogue's skill listing within 7,500 characters."
      Inference means "Plan each component against its rule: every skill body opens with the Codex bridge line, every agent declares a tools allowlist, no hook unless the plugin is in QUALIFIED_HOOKS and then exactly the qualified set, and the manifest's author an object with only a name and its license the catalogue's licence."
      Decision means "Name the reviewer now: someone other than the author of any part of the change. Route a change to QUALIFIED_HOOKS or another rule to the catalogue's owner as a decision, never as a side effect of the plugin change."
      Learning means "State which validator message each planned component could trigger, so a refusal is expected rather than discovered."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Make the change inside the plugin's folder and the catalogue's listing files only."
      Inference means "Run the catalogue's validator through the core's checker runner (check.mjs catalogue-validate, which runs python tools/validate.py in the catalogue) and read every message it prints."
      Decision means "Fix the plugin, never the validator, when it refuses; rerun until it passes, and keep each failed run on the record."
      Learning means "Report the validator's command, exit code and output verbatim."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Have the reviewer, who did not write the change, read it against the nine conventions and the validator output."
      Inference means "Qualify the plugin on its hosts with host-qualify: isolated install, strict validation, component inventory and listing cost."
      Decision means "Record the outcome: validator passed or refused, review findings and their resolution, and what remains unqualified on which host."
      Learning means "Propose a convention change to this part's steward when the validator's rule and its convention no longer agree."
